cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this app, please cite it and the works it builds on, listed under references.
type: software
title: bp-resp
abstract: Beat-to-beat arterial blood pressure (systolic, diastolic, beat-mean and pulse pressure, with pulse
  onsets found by the slope sum function of Zong et al. 2003), breathing (breath onsets, rate, amplitude,
  inspiration and expiration times with NeuroKit2), spontaneous baroreflex sensitivity by the sequence
  method (Bertinieri, Parati et al.) and the spectral alpha index and transfer-function gain (as compared
  in EuroBaVar), and respiratory sinus arrhythmia (peak-to-trough and Porges-Bohrer, NeuroKit2), for
  physiological recordings of humans and animals (species presets for human, pig, dog, rabbit, rat and
  mouse). Reads NWB files as written by physio-import, optionally stimulation epochs from stim-events and
  R-peaks from ecg-hrv; writes beat, breath and baroreflex tables and a regularly sampled series.csv for
  dose-response analysis. Uncalibrated pressure is used for timing only; recordings without pressure or
  respiration are reported as skipped. One step of the Heart Rate Variability and Baroreflex and the
  Cardiovascular Response to Nerve Stimulation workflows. Research outputs.
authors:
- name: Pennsieve (University of Pennsylvania)
contact:
- given-names: Joost
  family-names: Wagenaar
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-5925-5451
  affiliation: University of Pennsylvania
repository-code: https://github.com/pennsieve-apps/bp-resp
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
- physiology
- autonomic
- cardiovascular
- blood-pressure
- baroreflex
- respiration
- heart-rate-variability
- neuromodulation
- nwb
